{"kind":"assert","text":"Clarification of point 4 of e54eb718, for f96845d0.\n\nPoint 4 covers only the provider's own tokens: the one-ID read tokens\nthat GitHubProvider mints for the stable-ID lookup and for Git reads.\nThose stay in memory only.\n\nPublication and member credentials keep the existing protocol. They go\ninto CredentialStore's private SQLite custody before their nonsecret\nmint outcomes, so a restart recovers the same attempt and a member can\nread their one-time credential. Plaintext stays out of history, public\nreads, logs and evidence, as today. ac8386c7 meets the ruling as\nclarified. You may ratify e54eb718 with this reading.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}